         "From Mazaca Caesar marched towards Pontus. The author writes frankly about his army: the veteran sixth legion, which he had brought from Alexandria, numbered less than a thousand men because of so much fighting and marching; to this were added Deiotarus’ legion and two others that had taken part in Domitius’ battle (69). According to Ramsey and Raaflaub he reached Sebasteia on 13 May, where he gathered the four legions.\n\n"
